meta {
  name: Face Enroll
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/attendance/face/enroll
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "user_id": "{{userId}}",
    "consent": true
  }
}

docs {
  The reference photo is NOT sent here — it is the user's avatar, uploaded first
  via identity-service (POST /users/me/photo or /users/:id/photo). Enroll reads
  that stored photo, runs the in-process face engine (YuNet + SFace) and stores
  an AES-256-GCM-encrypted template in hr.face_templates.

  A member may enroll THEMSELVES (user_id === caller); hr_admin/org_admin may
  enroll anyone in-org. `consent` MUST be true (DPDP) — false returns 422
  FACE_CONSENT_REQUIRED. With no avatar on file: 400 FACE_NO_PHOTO. Self-service
  re-enrolment within the org's cooldown: 422 FACE_CHANGE_COOLDOWN (admins bypass).

  Enrolment quality gate (the photo must make a good reference):
    400 FACE_NO_FACE      no clear face found
    400 FACE_LOW_QUALITY  details.reason = multiple_faces | face_too_small |
                          not_frontal | blurry | too_dark | too_bright | low_contrast
                          (`error` carries a plain-language retake instruction)
    422 FACE_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE  engine failure or FACE_TEMPLATE_KEY not set
  Nothing is written unless a good template exists. face_subject_id in the
  response is the hr.face_templates row id; re-enrolling replaces that row.
}
